  "question": {
    "text": "Let $O$ be the origin, the point $A$ be $z_1=\\sqrt{3}+2 \\sqrt{2} i$, the point $B\\left(z_2\\right)$ be such that $\\sqrt{3}\\left|z_2\\right|=\\left|z_1\\right|$ and $\\arg \\left(z_2\\right)=\\arg \\left(z_1\\right)+\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "R9y5V",
      "text": "area of triangle ABO is $\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4RP7L",
      "text": "ABO is an obtuse angled isosceles triangle",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EtGh9",
      "text": "area of triangle ABO is $\\frac{11}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NjJzw",
      "text": "ABO is a scalene triangle",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ZTBSY1zNOMLe1r7QW1tWct0LYaWuSXEA0APhoARAPwM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& O A=\\left|z_1\\right|=\\sqrt{3+8}=\\sqrt{11} \\\\\n& \\text { and } O B=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\left|z_1\\right|=\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{3}} \\\\\n& A B^2=O A^2+O B^2-2 \\cdot O A \\cdot O B \\cos \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\\\\n& \\quad=11+\\frac{11}{3}-2 \\cdot \\frac{11}{\\sqrt{3}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad A B=\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{3}} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad \\text { Area of } \\triangle A B D=\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot O A \\cdot O B \\cdot \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\\\\n& \\quad=\\frac{11}{4 \\sqrt{3}} \\text { sq. units }\n\\end{aligned}$\nHere $O B=A B$ and $\\angle A=\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}$\n$\\therefore \\quad \\triangle A B D$ is an obtuse angled isosceles triangle.",
    "image": null
  },
